 "parsed": {
  "count": 1,
  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin alone is enough. Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and all three require stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs. These need admin_dc or admin_adfs, which come from escalate_dc or escalate_adfs, which need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. The only techniques that give those footholds are auth_dc and auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. With mfa:admin deployed the chain is cut, even though the attacker can still phish, pivot, reach the appserver and kerberoast stolen_admin. Zero controls is not enough, because with no defences the attacker can phish, pivot, take the appserver, kerberoast, authenticate to and escalate on the dc, dump dbadmin credentials, then take the db and exfiltrate."
 },
